# Core stack and workflow

## Stack (do not replace)

Next.js App Router, React, TypeScript strict, Tailwind CSS, Supabase (PostgreSQL/Auth/Storage/RLS), Stripe, Railway, Zod, React Hook Form, Vitest + React Testing Library.

Do not add major frameworks, infra, UI kits, or duplicate libraries without a proven need. No Vercel-only services.

## Mandatory feature order

```text
Database → Storage → Backend → Frontend → Tests
```

Skip a layer only when it is genuinely unaffected.

## Before editing

1. Read existing repo files; never guess tables, columns, contracts, or config.
2. Inspect real Supabase schema, migrations, RLS, and Storage when relevant.
3. Follow `docs/AGENT-PLAYBOOK.md` and `ARCHITECTURE.md`.

## Quality

- Prefer typed, secure, server-authoritative code over shortcuts.
- Avoid `any`, dead code, and premature abstractions.
- Preserve Railway standalone compatibility.
- Before claiming done: `npm run lint`, `typecheck`, `test`, and relevant `build`.
